# Scratch frames and sweep logs. Anything new is ignored, so no later pass is nagged
# into committing scratch by the stop hook again. Write scratch to the session
# scratchpad outside the repository instead.
#
# The 86 files that were tracked here are down to 20, by the owner's decision of
# 10 September ("purge if not needed"), which reverses his own of 9 September
# ("leave them and stop the bleeding") — that one was about stopping new scratch
# arriving, not about keeping what was there. The 20 that stay are the frames
# `docs/process/V11_RUN_RECORD.md` cites by name as the evidence for a claim, plus
# the measuring script that produced one set of them, because this project has
# already paid once for throwing a measuring script away (V9's). Removing files
# from HEAD does not shrink the history and the branch is not rewritten for
# housekeeping.
/scratchpad/
